  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1118 AM MDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nUpper cutoff low situated over the PacNW today will jog south today \nand tomorrow making it to northern AZ by late Tuesday, then crosses \nthe Four Corners and starts to lift out by Wednesday. Meanwhile, the \nupper ridge is over the Gulf of Mexico today and then re-centers \nitself over the southeastern US by mid-week. The rest of today \nthrough Wednesday will feature quiet conditions with near seasonable \nto warmer than average temperatures, some breeziness Tuesday but \nlighter breezes on Wednesday, and mostly dry conditions both days. \nSlight chances of storms Wednesday in southern Hudspeth county. \n\nStill expecting a potent cold front to push in from the Great Plains \nlate Thursday and into Friday. Winds may start shifting northerly in \nthe afternoon Thursday becoming breezy but after sunset is when the \nfront really pushes through. Expect a brisk Thursday night, \novernight, and through the day Friday. Windy to very windy \nconditions expected with northeast to easterly winds at 25-40 mph \nwith gusts to 60 mph possible. Windiest conditions will be over \nridge tops and west facing slopes like the Hueco Tanks, west El \nPaso, etc. A Wind Advisory will be needed with highest confidence\nbeing counties along the Int'l Border where the strongest belt of\nwinds are expected, as well as west facing slopes in El Paso and\nthe Hueco Tanks. Winds somewhat relax through the day Friday, but\nstill will be noticeably breezy. One location to watch out for \nFriday will be the Lordsburg Playa causing dust from the strong \nwinds. Models are starting to agree that the area will see some \nrain along with this cold front. Cloudcroft could potentially see \nsome flurries or a quick dusting of snow Friday morning. Similar \nhigh temperatures Saturday as what we'll see Friday (lowlands: low\nto mid 60s, mtns: 40s and low 50s). Still going to be windy late \nFriday and into Saturday morning. Winds relax through the \nafternoon but will stay breezy out west nearing the AZ border. \nThis may be another day to watch for blowing dust on the Lordsburg\nPlaya.",
